Package: mos-rauc-update
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mos build <mos@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: mos device-side update client
 rauc-verify walks a local TUF repository from a pinned trusted root, enforcing
 per-role thresholds, expiries and version pins against a persistent rollback
 state; rauc-update adds transport and policy on top of that same walk --
 metadata mirroring, compatibility selection from the signed release manifest,
 resumable bounded download, and the offline lockbox import.
 .
 The device identity these tools select against
 (/usr/share/mos/release-identity.env) is written by the image composition, not
 by this package: board, profile and the pool version are facts about the build
 that produced an image, and one archive is installed into images of several.
 .
 The pinned trust anchor is not shipped by this package either, and no
 mechanism ships one yet; docs/design/release-signing.md records the
 provisioning decision as open.
